  "name": "spec parser silently drops unknown top-level keys, losing content on --spec",
  "slug": "spec-parser-silently-drops-unknown-top-level-keys-losing-con",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "slop new --spec {\"details\":\"...\"} (meant details_md) parses as an object, so specSchema strips the unknown key and succeeds with an empty details_md — the prose is silently gone, not in details_md, meta, or a warning. The intended object->markdown fallback is nearly unreachable because every spec field is optional/defaulted.",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "Parsing a spec JSON object with top-level keys outside specSchema either preserves them (meta/passthrough), rejects with a clear error, or falls to the markdown path — never silently drops content",
      "A test asserts --spec with an unknown key does not lose the value"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/tickets/spec.ts:56-63",
      "src/core/entities/spec.ts:13-20 (all fields optional/defaulted)"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
